// @check
// @error Unknown property `set`
// REGRESSION (B6a, C2.2): a `Set<T>` is its OWN type — it must NOT leak the `Map`
// surface. Even though a set is internally a boolean-valued `{[T]: boolean}` hash
// map, its surface is `.add`/`.has`/`.delete`/`.length`/`.keys`/`.values`, so
// `.set`/`.get` do NOT resolve. This rejects `.set` (the worst leak — it let you store
// an arbitrary boolean "value" into what should be pure membership). `.get` is
// likewise gone (see the sibling case).
let s: Set<string> = Set()
s.set("a", true)
